course: dictionary
lesson: 4581
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Look at the words around them to find which meaning the writer wants. «Most bacteria are harmless or helpful, and your gut holds trillions of useful ones.» Here helpful means good for us, doing useful work.
explain: Helpful has two main meanings. A helpful person is willing to help others, like a friend who holds the door open. A helpful thing is useful and makes a job easier, like a helpful tip or diagram. Kind criticism is «specific and helpful», so it shows you what to improve.
explain: Test your meaning by putting it into the sentence. If «a helpful tip makes a problem easier» still makes sense with your meaning, you have chosen well. Helpful often comes with words like very, be or to, as in «very helpful» or «be helpful».
fact: Helpful is an adjective, so it describes a noun, such as a helpful pupil or a helpful tip.
fact: The forms are helpful, more helpful and most helpful.
fact: «Helpful» can describe a person who is willing to help others.
fact: «Helpful» can also describe something useful that makes a job easier, such as a helpful diagram.
fact: Common phrases: «very helpful», «helpful hint», «helpful tip», «be helpful» and «helpful to».
exercise: «Most bacteria are harmless or helpful, like those in your gut.» In this sentence, helpful means | Very loud and noisy | Hungry for food | *Useful and good for us | Left behind in a rush
exercise: Ella carries her new classmate's bag and shows her the way to the hall. Ella is | *Helpful | Noisy | Angry | Lazy
exercise: «Kind criticism is specific and helpful, like "I love the colours, maybe make the dog bigger?"» What does the writer say about this criticism? | *It is useful, so it helps you improve | It is not true | It is rude and unkind | It is very long
test: «The teacher said my drawing tip was very helpful.» Here helpful means | Lost in the hall | Loud and rough | Hungry for lunch | *Useful, and it makes the drawing easier
test: Which sentence uses helpful to describe a person? | Helpful bacteria live in your gut | The helpful hint made the sum easy | *The new girl was helpful and showed us around | The helpful diagram showed all the steps
exam: Mia reads, «A helpful tip makes a problem easier.» Which is closest to what helpful means here? | Slow and quiet | Kind to people | *Useful, making a job easier | Shiny and bright
